et":"zotero://select/library/items/AQ6S3FSE","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/3P76ISV5?page=1&annotation=ZU5XHDT7","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 5","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/3P76ISV5?page=5&annotation=ZGS5YRER","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/3P76ISV5?page=1&annotation=4VF9TQRI","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 17","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/3P76ISV5?page=17&annotation=KGTF6QHP","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Explainable deep learning ensemble for food image analysis on edge devices","Authors":"Ghalib Ahmed Tahir, Chu Kiong Loo","Year":2021,"DOI":"10.1016/j.compbiomed.2021.104972","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Thus, we proposed a user- centered explainable artificial intelligence (AI) framework to increase the trust of the involved parties by inferencing and rationalizing the results according to needs and user profile. Our framework is comprehensive in terms of a dietary assessment app as it detects Food/Non-Food, food categories, and ingredients.In this study, we proposed a three-fold method aimed to 1) detect food images thereby filtering irrelevant non-food images by the users, 2) classify these images according to food categories by recognizing food ingredients and 3) provide explanations using a user-centred explain­ able AI framework to improve the trust of all involved parties.","Findings":"Experimental results on the standard food benchmarks and newly contributed Malaysian food dataset for ingredient detection demonstrated superior performance on an integrated set of measures over other methodologie","Conclusions":"Furthermore, the current study also proposed a user-centred explainable AI framework that enhances the understanding of expla­ nations for all stakeholders. The results of the study confirm that our framework warrants the prediction results of the AI models based on user group type in improving the trust of AI experts, users, and di­ eticians. For future studies, we planned to evaluate the proposed framework using images with various quality distortio","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"kbk1ua","at":1774939670828}},"smart_blocks:tahirExplainableDeepLearning2021a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.0172656,0.03065662,-0.01902369,0.00106344,0.0588019,0.04863867,0.03213347,0.04177088,-0.02540858,-0.01388935,-0.00215304,-0.11112316,0.00793615,0.03629424,0.06407547,-0.0139446,0.00760314,0.00014623,-0.04374258,-0.06553561,0.05931473,-0.03041993,0.00542031,-0.03151634,-0.00049656,0.06757414,0.00713377,-0.0494477,-0.05567543,-0.24421574,0.0481526,-0.01955486,0.08431477,-0.05729537,-0.00488825,-0.00550767,-0.01586306,-0.00796517,-0.0354196,-0.0156626,0.02335677,-0.00320089,0.00718029,0.00149065,0.00720335,-0.02716042,-0.08196474,-0.02771164,-0.09640609,-0.03046936,0.02041506,-0.03331627,0.00940096,0.05536219,0.03671658,0.03493765,0.03281477,0.03966832,0.02957032,0.07514711,0.01996675,0.05922735,-0.16075151,0.06306508,0.05493745,-0.01374041,-0.02985079,-0.00836924,-0.02577841,-0.01306155,-0.00546717,0.06912434,0.0703015,0.01149892,0.01314626,-0.00649432,0.07085879,-0.04969972,-0.03132368,-0.02468129,0.00395674,0.09698524,0.01162337,-0.03325846,-0.0217053,-0.02371844,-0.00488456,-0.0626931,0.02434478,-0.03303794,-0.0049836,0.0108341,-0.02401961,-0.0044677,0.00023761,-0.0160204,-0.02817732,-0.01603385,-0.07027039,0.11175267,-0.05432029,-0.03488537,-0.0104069,-0.02397709,-0.00441585,-0.00730484,-0.05079696,-0.02802062,0.00399265,0.04079514,-0.0502948,0.01775012,-0.01531901,0.00333465,-0.01488108,0.0206282,0.0879277,0.00627047,0.04013466,-0.04442327,-0.03301984,0.03213941,0.03916776,-0.00262078,-0.0146985,0.04795495,-0.00377846,0.08489004,-0.00227377,0.01249971,0.08088204,-0.02803532,-0.07540622,0.0247